[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"729","stub":{"id":"729","section":"2) Jerusalem Mill (Jerusalem Rd.) to U.S. Route 40","altname":"","river":"Little Gunpowder Falls","difficulty":"IItoIII","states":["USA-MRY"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"17","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"Put-in is at the Jerusalem Mill Historic Area at the Jerusalem Rd. Little Gunpowder Falls bridge.","id":"106881","location":{"latitude":"39.46220409","longitude":"-76.39134757"},"name":"Jerusalem Mill Put-in","distance":"0","photoID":"42364","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"The first take-out for the run - the take-out usually used by Baltimore Area paddlers","id":"106885","location":{"latitude":"39.42428355","longitude":"-76.37753671"},"name":"Philadelphia Rd. (MD 7) Take-out","distance":"3.37","photoID":"0","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"Lower take-out which can be used if parking is limited at Philadelphia Rd.","id":"106886","location":{"latitude":"39.42148704","longitude":"-76.37305345"},"name":"US 40 Take-out","distance":"3.7","photoID":"0","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"101254232","title":null,"post_date":"2019-05-13 04:00:00+00","detail":"Rapid \"Rock Island,\" described in the alert below from 3 months ago, as of 5/12/19 also had a large tree significantly obstructing the left (and only remaining) channel. It may be possible to duck under the tree, depending on the water level, but it is a difficult move involving a tricky eddy, a Class III maneuver immediately after ducking, and high consequences for failure. The obstruction calls for careful scouting and assessment.","user":{"name":"Larry Lempert"}},{"id":"101254058","title":null,"post_date":"2019-02-01 05:00:00+00","detail":"Rapid \"Rock Island\" currently has a large tree across the right slot. You can scout from the eddy above it on river right, leaving only the left slot to be the move to make. From the river right eddy you can see some of the left drop but be aware and maybe get out and scout for any wood past what you can only boat scout.","user":{"name":"Keith Trotta"}},{"id":"100058922","title":null,"post_date":"2011-09-08 04:00:00+00","detail":"Labor Day 2011 three of us scooted and ran the Little Gunpowder. Or should I say walked and knuckle\ndragged our way down the river. At low water its point less to even attempt. We tried removing\nthe large steel re-bar hazard but proved to massive to remove. In turn it was re-bar was pinned\ndown under a boulder. Looks like a great creek a higher levels. According to our GPS total distance\nHarford Road to Rt 40 is 7.5 miles not 5.5 miles as stated on the main page for Little Gunpowder","user":null},{"id":"101247527","title":null,"post_date":"2010-12-16 05:00:00+00","detail":"Ran this last weekend after a decent day of rain. Gauge only spiked at 250cfs, it was maybe 200 when we went through. The big flood storm that came through a few months ago definitely changed some scenery. The banks are wider and the \"islands\" between Jerusalem and Franklinville were all but swept clean. At this level, the run was bony but we only scraped a couple times and all of the drops were runnable. One thing to note is that after the Jerusalem Road put in there is a huge near-river-wide strainer which backs up a lot of water and creates its own little rapid, passable with a tight slot move on the right but take it slow and watch for protruding branches in the slide.","user":{"name":"Douglas Engle"}},{"id":"100058240","title":null,"post_date":"2007-09-27 04:00:00+00","detail":"This river is NOT runnable at 1.93 feet / 84 CF/s. We just went down and tried it thinking it would just be a 'little low'. We were only able to paddle about 200 yards of the first 3 miles. We had to hike along the trails and take out at Jerusalem Road bridge and hitch a ride back to the putgtin to get our vehicle. Locals told us that the river is usually a full foot higher. I would say 2.5 feet would be runnable, with 3 feet preferable. Oh well....","user":null}],"photos":[{"id":"42364","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"10134","description":"Jerusalem Road Put-in","caption":"Little Gunpowder Put-in","poi_name":"Put-in","subject":"Jerusalem Mill Putin","author":"Coop","poi_id":"106881","photo_date":null,"updated_at":"2023-07-09T14:10:32.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/42364","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/42364"}},{"id":"42368","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"10136","description":"","caption":"Belko Factory Falls","poi_name":"Belko Factory Falls","subject":"Mark Cooper","author":"","poi_id":"106883","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/42368","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/42368"}},{"id":"10180","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7041","description":"","caption":"first drop below bridge","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"stevef","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10180","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10180"}},{"id":"10183","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7041","description":"","caption":"2nd drop river left","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"steve f","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10183","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10183"}},{"id":"10181","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7041","description":"","caption":"2nd drop below bridge river left","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"steve f","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10181","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10181"}},{"id":"10184","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7041","description":"","caption":"2nd drop center channel","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"steve f","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10184","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10184"}},{"id":"10185","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7041","description":"","caption":"2nd drop river rt","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"steve f","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10185","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10185"}},{"id":"10186","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7041","description":"","caption":"2nd drop center channel","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"steve f","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10186","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10186"}},{"id":"10187","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7041","description":"","caption":"2nd drop river left","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"steve f","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10187","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10187"}},{"id":"10188","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7041","description":"","caption":"3rd drop","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"steve f","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10188","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10188"}},{"id":"10179","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7042","description":"","caption":"Below covered bridge","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"stevef","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10179","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10179"}},{"id":"12456","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8916","description":"","caption":"Gunpowder Run","poi_name":"","subject":"Nate Shils","author":"Lee Thonus","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/12456","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/12456"}},{"id":"42366","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"10134","description":"Nice \"creek-like\" triple drop on the Little Gunpowder.","caption":"Triple Drop","poi_name":"Triple Drop","subject":"Ken ","author":"Coop","poi_id":"0aNSJNuEnLveM6vMOLYs4","photo_date":null,"updated_at":"2023-09-25T14:46:30.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/42366","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/42366"}},{"id":"42367","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"10137","description":"","caption":"First Ledge Little Gunpowder","poi_name":"First Drop on Little Gunpowder","subject":"Coop","author":"?","poi_id":"106887","photo_date":null,"updated_at":"2023-07-09T14:09:09.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/42367","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/42367"}}],"detail":{"id":"729","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"This is the delightful, classic Little Gunpowder trip. The first mile is an almost continuous rock garden, starting out class I-II and then adding a few class II and II+ bits.  Then, in short succession, come a series of class III rapids. The first is a 3-4-foot ledge, easily boat scouted and best run in the middle at most levels. It is popular to carry back up and run it again. The next splits around an island, with the left side narrower and shallower. Then comes the Belko Factory Falls, a ragged 5-6-foot drop which can be scouted from the left and run on the right. The remaining class II+ rapids, above the Franklintown Rd. bridge, are twisty rock gardens. Class II water then resumes, down to I-95. The final mile and a half has only a pair of class II rapids on either side of Philadelphia Road, a half-mile above US 40.\n\nEarly on, the trip features a covered bridge for the paddler to pass under.  The surrounding woodlands are full of deer and quite pretty, except where buildings are close to the creek. You can park at the shopping center alongside the take out. If you continue below there, it is two flat miles to the big Gunpowder Falls, and then another mile to the Gunpowder River inlet.\n\nEd Evangelidi testifies:\n\nThis creek is quite flashy, so don't dawdle, or it might come down on you while you are running shuttle. It has more continuous rapids than on the Big Gunpowder but they are not any harder. Also has a tamer section upstream.\n\nLat/longitude coords are approximate, from TopoZone.","averageGradient":"33","maxGradient":"75","length":"3.7","correlations":[{"reachID":"729","isPrimary":false,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"101","beginMediumRunnable":"150","beginHighRunnable":"800","endHighRunnable":"2345"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"WINTERS RUN NEAR BENSON, MD","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"01581700","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"17","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"1.33","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"39.51994444","longitude":"-76.37297222"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/01581700","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/01581700/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},